# template.domain-term

shape of a `choice._.` cluster under `.agent/repo=.this/role=any/briefs/domain.terms/`. one cluster per term, reused across every dobj/dop it composes.

```
term=<boundary…>.<x>._.choice._.md               # SAY — data only, no forbid prose
term=<boundary…>.<x>._.choice.reason.md          # REF — REQUIRED
term=<boundary…>.<x>._.choice.example=<abc>.md   # REF — optional, one per example
```

```md
# domain.term: stone

term.chosen   = stone
term.kind     = noun          # noun | verb | adj
term.boundary = route         # REQUIRED
term.synonyms.forbidden:
- checkpoint

## .what
a single milestone on a route.

## .refs
- src/domain.objects/Stone.ts

## .reason
- `term=route.stone._.choice.reason.md`
```

reason file: `## .etymology` (why this word, over which rejected) · `## .disputes` (`### dispute: <word> — raised YYYY-MM-DD — status: RESOLVED (<outcome>)` with raised.by / claim / counter / resolution) · `## .evidence` (discovery; invariants if a dobj).

example file: `# domain.term.choice.example: <term> — <slug>`, a short demo.

dispute pattern: `howto.domain-term-disputes`.
